  "erasComment": "The helmets by era (docs/HISTORIKER.md, third pre-check; the historiker's helmet pre-check and post-check of 29 October 2026). Rank 1 (Dorf) stays in the first era on purpose. The sallet north of the Alps only from about 1440, so the German crossbowman keeps the cervelliere until rank 4; the archers take a helmet from 1400 on. The German sallet is worn only with its bevor (post-check: alone its face is too open). An era begins with a rank of the village, not with a year: the game's years are short and a village should see its men re-armed as it grows. The Hundsgugel stays German (thin in England and France), the great bascinet western, the German sallet with its bevor the Empire's, the Burgundian sallet with its bevor (in the one layer, as drawn) England's and France's. The great helm is not offered: a village levy in one is wrong (knights only). Celata, armet and barbuta are drawn but not given to anyone by default: Italian, and rare; they wait for the player's own choice at the muster. Spearman and archer keep the kettle hat and the coif throughout: the common man's helmets did not change as fast.",
